    {
      "id": "claim_7f0d1f9e759741048b3cf42db9a3a000",
      "statement": "StubEmbedder namespaces its model id as `stub:<model>` so a stub vector and a live vector can never share an embed_key; without the prefix a collection seeded under stub and re-ingested under gemini reused every hash vector and reported them as reused while buying no embedding.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/ingest/embed.py#L397-L418",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e185efdc300f6375f064294b5f774d72eb7ea233a48318e137d5a530ec04d2e4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6014ce1677574686b6d1860df1e0bb65",
      "statement": "Both live backends build their SDK client lazily behind a lock, because the embedding step fans batches out over a thread pool and an unguarded lazy build lets a second thread orphan the first client, closing the transport under a worker mid-run.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/ingest/embed.py#L478-L491",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:187f5b9454b31fd2b9e094369b573ea5eba8fc8325de1ce62683b5a0974ef3a4:"
